# {{.ID}}

A LastERP server plugin (`{{.Lang}}`), targeting `{{.ABIVersion}}`.

Read `manifest.yaml` first — it is the whole of what this plugin may do, and
what an administrator approves at install. A capability it does not list is a
host function this module cannot import, so the sandbox refuses to instantiate
it rather than refusing the call.

## Build, pack, install

See the header of the source file for the build command for this language, then:

```sh
lasterp plugin pack -manifest manifest.yaml -module plugin.wasm -key publisher.key -out {{.Name}}.tar.gz
lasterp plugin install ./{{.Name}}.tar.gz -server $LASTERP_URL -token $LASTERP_TOKEN
```

`lasterp plugin keygen` makes `publisher.key` and prints the line an operator
adds to their trust file. A deployment installs no bundle it cannot verify.

## Typed bindings for your tenant's objects

```sh
lasterp plugin bindings -server $LASTERP_URL -token $LASTERP_TOKEN -out objects.go
```

The full walkthrough is in the LastERP docs: `docs/23-PLUGIN-TUTORIAL.md`.
